# Projects

Hands-on data projects built with Python, covering data cleaning, analysis, and interactive visualization. Several were completed as part of my IBM Data Analyst certification.

## What's Inside

| Project | Description | Tools |
|---|---|---|
| `airline-delay-dashboard` | Interactive web dashboard that lets users enter a year and instantly see average monthly flight arrival delays as a line chart | Python, Pandas, Plotly, Dash |
| `auto-data-cleaning` | Cleaned and prepared a raw automobile dataset for analysis by detecting missing values, imputing them, and standardizing data types | Python, Pandas, NumPy |

---

### ✈️ Airline Performance Dashboard
An interactive dashboard built with Plotly Dash on a real US airline performance dataset.

- User enters a year in an input box
- A callback filters the data to that year and calculates average arrival delay by month
- Results render as a live line chart that updates on every input

**Skills shown:** interactive dashboards, callbacks, data filtering and aggregation (`groupby`), data visualization

---

### 🚗 Automobile Data Cleaning
Data wrangling on a raw automobile dataset with missing and inconsistent values, preparing it for downstream analysis or modeling.

- Replaced placeholder `?` values with proper nulls and counted missing values per column
- Filled missing numeric values (normalized losses, bore, stroke, horsepower, peak RPM) with the column mean
- Filled missing categorical values (number of doors) with the most common value
- Dropped rows missing the target variable (price), since they can't be used for price prediction
- Converted columns to correct data types (int, float) for accurate calculations

**Skills shown:** data quality assessment, missing-value imputation strategies, data type correction, data preparation

